{{/*
  check-behind-base — verify the current branch is not behind its target base
  before pushing, and STOP if it is. Consumed by prompts that push commits to
  an existing PR (fix-ci, address-pr-comments, submit-changes) and that must
  not rebase inline. Prevents "green locally, red in CI" surprises caused by
  missing recent base commits.

  Composes git/shared/behind-base-count (the detection) with a stop-and-defer
  verdict. Prompts that DO rebase inline (git/commit-and-submit) consume
  behind-base-count directly instead.

  Preconditions: the caller has already resolved `<target-remote>` and
  `<target-branch>` (usually via the git/identify-remote-branch fragment) OR
  will infer them inline with `gh pr view --json baseRefName` when a PR pins
  the target.

  Callers should place this fragment under a numbered step heading of their
  choice (e.g. "### 4. Check if Rebase Needed").
*/}}
{{ template "git/shared/behind-base-count" . }}
{{- if and .Session.IsLoop (not .Session.IsLoopForced) }}

**Scheduled mode**: do not attempt to rebase inline (conflicts mid-fix are
unsafe when unattended). Instead, `mitto_ui_notify` (`warning`, `sound: true`)
that the branch is `<N>` commits behind `<target-remote>/<target-branch>` and
needs a rebase before the fix can be pushed, then stop. The outer supervisor
(e.g. `babysit-this-pr`) or a human will rebase and re-trigger this run.
{{- else }}

**Interactive mode**: inform the user that the branch is behind and defer to
the **"Rebase changes"** prompt. Do not rebase inline from this prompt — the
dedicated rebase workflow handles conflict resolution properly. Stop after
notifying so the user (or a follow-up run) can rebase first.
{{- end }}
